<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#cognateTerms> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Terms in related languages that are etymologically cognate or semantically parallel. Used to document cross-tradition vocabulary relationships (e.g., Yorùbá 'Egúngún' → Lucumí 'Eggun'; Fon 'Legba' → Haitian 'Legba')."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#secretNameText> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The secret name itself. No-access: never exported to RDF, stored internally for provenance only."@en .
