<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#lang-african-christian> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Languages of African origin used in pre-colonial or early-colonial African Christian traditions. Ge'ez (Ethiopian Orthodox, Eritrean Orthodox), Coptic (Egyptian Coptic Church). Included here because of their continuity with African sacred language traditions and their presence in Afro-Atlantic communities."@en .
