<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#lang-full-liturgical> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A language used in its complete grammatical form as the primary medium of sacred communication. Examples: Yorùbá in continental Yorùbá religion; Fon in Beninese Vodun; Ge'ez in Ethiopian Orthodox liturgy."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#SpeechActTypeScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#act-invocation> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#script-oral-only> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Language transmitted exclusively orally without a writing system. The majority of Afro-Atlantic liturgical languages fall here historically; Latin transcription is secondary."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#act-blessing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
