<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#lang-afro-atlantic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A source language preserved in Afro-Atlantic in a fossilized or adapted form, used for liturgical purposes but no longer a community vernacular. Examples: Lucumí (Afro-Atlantic Yorùbá in Cuba); Kikongo as used in Cuban Palo Monte; liturgical Fon in Haitian Vodou."@en .
