<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#hasPhrase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a SacredLanguage to a LiturgicalPhrase expressed in that language. Inverse of iroko:phraseLanguage. Enables a researcher to start from a language and traverse its attested liturgical formulas, invocations, greetings, and oaths. Access: community-only — attested liturgical phrases are appropriate for practitioners and qualified scholars; phrase translations and full texts are governed at initiated level on the LiturgicalPhrase instances themselves."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#esotericDefinition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#LexicalSense> .
